WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.573
- You look sharp, you know that?

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.500
Like comin' out, is that Gucci?

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
I recognize that strip, that
looks nice, that looks nice.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.100
It's like 90's, I love that about Gucci.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.340
- Shout out to Dapper Dan.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.680
- Yes, Rick has songs about sunglasses.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.120
You have your own sunglass
collection, right?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.090
- I do, I have, I collect my own, yes.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.150
- Oh I love it, I love it, okay.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.030
So he's never seen without
sunglasses, which I love.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.060
Basically he's known for
his sunglasses y'all.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.011
So, what's with the sunglasses?

00:00:31.011 --> 00:00:33.330
- It could go back to me as a youngster.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.570
When I was a youngster
in elementary school,

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.240
a lot of my friends used to pick on me

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.120
because of the length of my eyelashes.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.483
- Wait, are they like really long?

00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:45.724
(laughs)

00:00:45.724 --> 00:00:46.807
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:47.794 --> 00:00:51.223
- Let me see, they're beautiful.

00:00:51.223 --> 00:00:54.190
See, this is what ticks me off about men.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:55.464
They are wasted.

00:00:55.464 --> 00:00:59.544
I have these short, I have
these short stubby little like,

00:00:59.544 --> 00:01:01.760
and then pregnancy ruined it even more.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.570
It's like, I don't understand,
I have to wear lashes,

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.863
these ain't, nothin' on me is mine.

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:09.320
And those are just natural
and you're hiding it.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:10.873
I'm upset with you Rick Ross.

00:01:10.873 --> 00:01:12.860
- And as a youngster I hated 'em.

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.130
- Oh really?
- I did.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.090
- They're so beautiful, but
I do like the shades too,

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:18.800
it's rock 'n roll, I'm
into it, I'm into it.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.220
So I thought it might be fun,

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.917
since you love sunglasses,
you're known for it,

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.790
I thought it might be fun to try on

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.060
like a few iconic frames,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:27.893
see how they look on you.

00:01:27.893 --> 00:01:28.817
Are you cool with that?

00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:29.650
- I'm with it.

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:31.720
- All right, all right,
come on out here, elf.

00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:38.167
He's like the most miserable elf.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:41.881
(laughs)

00:01:43.175 --> 00:01:45.173
It's great, great.

00:01:47.057 --> 00:01:49.998
He is killin' that Christmas spirit.

00:01:49.998 --> 00:01:52.900
All right, all right, let's
ease into it, shall we?

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.780
Okay, I think you're
gonna go with these first.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.730
These are, they kinda
look like U2, like Bono,

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:58.870
a little Bono-esque.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:00.780
So, let's try these.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.010
- Make some noise for Bono.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.160
- Exactly, I love Bono.

00:02:05.077 --> 00:02:06.023
Let's see, yeah.

00:02:06.885 --> 00:02:09.728
(applause)

00:02:09.728 --> 00:02:10.768
- Those look good on you.

00:02:10.768 --> 00:02:12.990
- Yes, they do look good on you.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.729
Okay, okay, well this one,

00:02:14.729 --> 00:02:17.530
this is I think Oprah has been rockin'

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.380
a bold look like these, these days.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.430
So I mean, if it's good for Oprah,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.665
it's good for all of us, right?

00:02:22.665 --> 00:02:24.526
- Make some noise for Oprah.

00:02:24.526 --> 00:02:26.776
(applause)

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.270
- You look good in sunglasses.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.285
You have like the perfect
shaped head, I'm not kidding.

00:02:35.285 --> 00:02:39.850
I have to go for a specific
style or it's like nope.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.010
Okay, we're gonna go for these,

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.640
obviously these are a little Elton John,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.894
make some noise for Elton John.

00:02:44.894 --> 00:02:49.894
These are a little flashy, little flashy.

00:02:52.449 --> 00:02:54.532
(laughs)

00:02:57.188 --> 00:03:00.071
(cheers)

00:03:00.071 --> 00:03:01.238
You look good.

00:03:02.121 --> 00:03:03.940
- Y'all got me good, y'all got me good.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.820
- Which one is your
favorite if you had to pick?

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.523
Cause I'm just sayin'
the bedazzle is nice.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.170
- I may go with these.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.749
- Oh, you're goin' the Oprah one, I see.

00:03:14.749 --> 00:03:17.097
You can't go wrong, you can't go wrong.

00:03:17.097 --> 00:03:19.779
You gonna rock those for
the rest of the show?

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:22.287
You don't have to, yours
are pretty cool too.

00:03:22.287 --> 00:03:24.640
But let's seriously, let's
talk about your book,

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.880
cause you have a memoir out,
it's called Hurricanes, right?

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:27.930
- Hurricanes, yes.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.200
- So, what's it about?

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.020
- It's really just talkin' 'bout my rise,

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:35.180
you know, my rise to where I
am today as a artist, you know.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.240
Just lettin' you know that
we all love the sunshine,

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.500
but you will deal with hurricanes in life,

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.010
and just, you gotta deal with 'em,

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.150
you gotta deal with 'em and move forward.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.950
You know I'm comin' into album number 10,

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.257
you have to challenge
yourself creative-wise,

00:03:50.257 --> 00:03:52.650
and I wanted to bring
somethin' else to the game,

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.770
and a different perspective.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.450
So, me tellin' everyone
just my straight-from-me,

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:00.280
my voice, and I felt it'd
blow a lotta people's minds,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.600
and I wanted to come out with the album.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.251
The album went number one, so,

00:04:04.251 --> 00:04:06.171
it's just a lotta dope touchin'.

00:04:06.171 --> 00:04:08.600
- That's so awesome, I'm so happy for you.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.213
And it's awesome, I think too,

00:04:10.213 --> 00:04:13.040
for fans just to get like
inside your heart and head,

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.120
and that's why I like to be a songwriter.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.490
I like singing songs that I didn't write,

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.390
but I also love to write,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.760
cause it gives people the opportunity

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.017
to kinda see who you are.

00:04:20.017 --> 00:04:21.290
- All the time, all the time.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.260
- So, I actually heard that
you were recently nominated

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.093
for a Grammy, right?

00:04:24.093 --> 00:04:27.740
- I am.
- Yes, that's exciting.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.677
- I am Grammy nominated,

00:04:29.677 --> 00:04:32.490
for the record Single Gold
Roses featuring Drake,

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:33.958
one time for Drake.

00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:35.300
- Yeah, I loved it.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.450
- And for me, what makes this moment

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.020
even that much more special is

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.780
the record was actually conceived

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:45.090
from a conversation me and
Drake had over Nipsey Hussle.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.810
You know, rest in peace to Nipsey Hussle.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.280
It was a conversation that we had,

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.040
and we was just speakin' about,

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.550
you have to, a lotta times,

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:57.270
let's celebrate a person's
energy while they're still here

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:00.330
to accept it, you know, and
that's what it was about.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.141
- I love that too, the sense
of being the greatest record,

00:05:03.141 --> 00:05:03.974
the greatest song.

00:05:03.974 --> 00:05:06.070
Have you finished your holiday shopping?

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.430
- I haven't, I haven't.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.280
- You are, you, the clock is tickin'.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.820
- Yeah, the clock is tickin',

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:13.920
and, you know, it feels
like you never finish

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.600
when you have four little
beautiful children.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.330
- Me too, I feel as well,
it's like it's never,

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.970
I still think I'm done, and then I'm like,

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.450
wait did I even it out?

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:23.370
Cause they count, they count the gifts,

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:24.900
like they got more than me.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:27.340
- And not only that, it's,
you know, four in the mornin',

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.240
it's like Amazon is just
knockin' at your phone.

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:32.440
- Oh my gosh, but are you
stressed about the holidays?

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.170
Do you get stressed about it, both of you?

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.240
- I try not to.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.490
- You don't get stressed,
do you get stressed?

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:37.670
- I'm totally stressed.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.240
- I get stressed, I think the
momma's get super stressed.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.210
We feel like we're the one's
people are gonna look at

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.783
and be like it wasn't great.

00:05:45.154 --> 00:05:47.790
- Yeah, and we gotta cook too.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:51.170
- Oh, I'm a sous-chef, my
sister does that, yeah.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:53.420
My sister's like solid in a kitchen.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.133
I am solid at eating in a kitchen.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.440
Yeah, I am good at it, I rock it.

